(a) `app.json` is a Node.js experimental configuration file, not a general-purpose JavaScript file.\
(b) The option belongs inside the `nodeOptions` object:
```
{
  "nodeOptions": {
    "watch": true
  }
}
```

Thus, `watch` is not normally read when placed directly at the top level.\
(c) It is not an ordinary JavaScript module executed by Node. It is parsed as configuration data according to Node’s configuration-file schema. JavaScript expressions, imports, and arbitrary executable code are not run from this JSON file.

